  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "Transaction **TX-0401** is confirmed in your account ACC-1005:\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 20 July 2026\n- **Type:** Card payment, outgoing, status settled\n\nI also see **TX-0402**, which is EUR 240.00 to the same merchant on 14 July 2026, also settled. Two identical charges to the same merchant may be relevant if you think you were billed twice.\n\nThese reason codes could apply to a card payment like this one:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 could fit this if you only intended to pay once.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** You did not authorise the payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** Your card details were used without your permission for an online purchase.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid, but the item was never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid, but the service was never provided.\n\nWhich of these fits depends on what happened. Tell me, and I will check whether the transaction is eligible for a dispute under that code before anything is filed. I will not open a dispute without your confirmation.",
